---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WorkList from '../components/WorkList.astro';

const entries = (await getCollection('work', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .slice(0, 3);
---

<Base
  title="Sara Johnson — Senior Technical Product Manager"
  description="Senior technical product manager with eleven years as a working developer."
>
  <header class="intro">
    <h1>Product manager who spent eleven years writing the code first.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A one-paragraph positioning statement: the kind of product problems you take on, the stage of
      company you do it at, and what the engineering background actually buys the team.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="meta">01</span>
      <h2 id="work-heading">Selected work</h2>
    </div>
    <WorkList entries={entries} />
    <p class="more"><a href="/work/">All work →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="eng-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="meta">02</span>
      <h2 id="eng-heading">Before product</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      The thesis paragraph: why eleven years of shipping code makes you a better product manager, in
      concrete terms rather than as a credential.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/engineering/">What the engineering years bought →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="meta">03</span>
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Where to reach you, and what you're currently looking for.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--section-gap);
  }

  .intro h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: var(--section-gap);
  }

  .section-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--size-small);
  }
</style>
